  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "When the mind is content it has acquired the power of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "चिन्तामणि; for having nothing to wish for it can be said that it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "has given itself all that it longs for. विमुक्तः संकल्पः &c.—When",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "all desires have been foregone, every desire has in fact been",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "gratified. Cf. Gita II. 70, 79. यदा सर्वे प्रमुच्यन्ते कामा येस्य हृदि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "स्थिताः । अथ मर्त्योऽमृतो भवत्यत्र ब्रह्म समश्नुते ॥ Kathop. 2. 3, 14.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 63. स्वयम् &c.—The line gives expression to fatalism. Cf.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "यदभावि न तद्भावि भावि चेन्न तदन्यथा । इति चिन्ताविषघ्नोयमगदः किं न",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "पीयते ॥ H. I. The line may also be interpreted as–things happen",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "in the best way when they are allowed their natural way. They",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "are not brought about so well by exertions. असंकल्पयन्—not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "forming anticipations or expectations. अनुभवस्व—भू ' to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "with अनु is Par; so this must be taken as a form of भू to get or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "obtain which is P. A.; or separate अनुभव स्वभोगान्.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 64. आयासक–troublesome; goes with गहनात्. विरम् governs",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the abl. of the object from which cessation is meant. श्रेयोमार्गम्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "(the obj. of आश्रय in l. 1.)—the path of final beatitude. अतिशयेन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "प्रशस्यं श्रेयः what is most to be praised–hence sought, i. e. मोक्ष;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "मुक्तिः कैवल्यनिर्वाणंश्रेयोनिःश्रेयसामृतम् । मोक्षोपवर्गः—Amara. क्षणात् goes",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with शमन. शान्तं भावं which is necessary for entering on the श्रेयो-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मार्ग. गति course, movements. Cf. विधिगतीः sl. 87 Infra. भूयः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "again, with persistence.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 65. Addressed to the mind. मार्गय Imper, 2nd sing.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Some read मोहं मार्जयताम्—of those who have swept away infatu-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "ation. ताम् in our reading means प्रसिद्धाम्. तटभुवाम् of the grounds",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "on the bank. आसङ्गमङ्गीकुरु–resort to the vicinity of. को वा प्रत्ययः-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "what faith can be placed ? the answer being 'none.' स्त्रीषु श्रीषु v. l.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "may equally do. Cf. अपण्डितास्ते पुरुषा मता मे ये स्त्रीषु च श्रीषु च",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "विश्वसन्ति । पन्नग-पन्नं पतितं यथा तथा गच्छतीति.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 66. आस्था—earnestness. भूपाल०—Fortune very often",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "depends upon the royal favour a man enjoys and its stability or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "otherwise is to be determined from a look of pleasure or a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "frown that the king's face wears. Lakshmî is, therefore, com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "pared to a dancing girl dancing in imitation of the movements",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
